cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper and this repository."
title: "motif-faithfulness-audit: code, processed data and results of a stability and counterfactual audit of motif-level explanations in cell-conditioned multi-omics drug response prediction"
authors:
  - family-names: Abdelhaliem
    given-names: Amr H.
    email: amrcs2014@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Department of Cyber Security, Faculty of Science and Information Technology, Irbid National University, Irbid, Jordan"
version: "1.0.3"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/amrcs2014-pixel/motif-faithfulness-audit"
keywords:
  - drug response prediction
  - explainable AI
  - graph neural networks
  - counterfactual explanations
  - multi-omics
  - GDSC
  - DepMap
abstract: >-
  Code, processed data and summary results of a stability and counterfactual audit of
  motif-level explanations produced by a CCMG-class (cell-conditioned motif graph) model for drug
  response prediction on GDSC2 x DepMap. Five motif-level and four gene-level explainers are scored
  for seed, regime and input-noise stability, for faithfulness against motif deletion/swap and gene
  knockdown counterfactuals, and against drug-target biology, with DrEval-style baselines, attention
  and tuning controls, positive-control biomarkers, curated pharmacophores and a planted-importance
  sanity check.
